# MER-237: deploy the public site and nothing else.
#
# Vercel uploads and serves every repository file that is not ignored here, so before this file
# existed orbgss.com also served STATUS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/, tasks/, evidence/, scripts/ and hero/.
# This is an allowlist (https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/vercel-ignore#allowlist): the first rule
# ignores everything at the repository root, and each following "!" line re-includes one public
# root entry, whole. A new public page or top-level file must be added here, or it will not be
# deployed. scripts/validate_site.py parses this file and fails if a public page references
# anything outside it, if an internal path is let back in, or if an entry names nothing.
#
# vercel.json is project configuration (clean URLs, headers, caching); Vercel reads it but does not
# serve it.

/*
!index.html
!404.html
!styles.css
!script.js
!site.webmanifest
!robots.txt
!sitemap.xml
!vercel.json
!assets
!platform
!solutions
!pilot
!company
!contact
